  "body": "Side branch: side/path-kernel\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/4254#issuecomment-7207515978 (worker K4c-air-approach).\n\n## What changed\n\nA stay-down link can now end with an approach from the air. The approach is a straight stretch from the nearest place of the air to the start of an open piece on a stock edge loop. The link stage proves it. The plan has no new step kind, and the transition table of `Plan::new` does not change.\n\n- `crates/pathkernel/src/link/approach.rs` (new): the approach proof and the fourth try of the link (`from_air`).\n- `crates/pathkernel/src/link/proof.rs`: the chord proof is split into its room test, its crossing test and its swath test. The three tries of K4 are now one function (`tries`), so that the way out to the air uses them.\n- `crates/pathkernel/src/link/route.rs`: `project` is visible to the link module.\n- The order stage does not change (decision 4 in the record).\n\n## The rule\n\nThe next cut must be an open piece whose start is on a stock edge loop. The approach starts at the place of an air loop nearest to that start, within a tool radius. The approach holds only when all of these are true:\n\n- Each sample is in the air or the edge band, out of the part zone, more than a tool radius from each keep-out area, and not inside the cutter-centre area.\n- The stretch holds in the legal room of the entry stage.\n- The stretch crosses no cut made and no link, and touches no planned cut away from the ends of the link.\n- The disc swept along the stretch, less the swath of the next piece, lies within a tool radius of the air. The air starts one tool radius outside the stock, so that rest is outside the stock.\n\nThus each piece of stock that the approach cuts is also cut by the next piece. The test is exact polygon geometry. Its only tolerance is the polygon flattening (`AREA_TOL`, 2 x `ROOM_TOL` = 10 um). No strip of uncut stock is open by a constant.\n\nA piece whose start is not on a stock edge keeps the present rule. Where no proof holds, the link lifts with the reason of the straight link.\n\n## Pins\n\nNegative pins first (`crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/air_approach.rs`, in the `laws` directory suite):\n\n- `an_approach_that_would_cut_stock_off_the_curve_is_refused`: a tooth of stock beside the start. A mutation run without the area test makes this pin fail.\n- `an_approach_near_a_keep_out_at_the_stock_edge_is_refused`\n- `an_approach_beside_a_part_that_reaches_out_of_the_stock_is_refused`\n- `a_piece_that_does_not_start_at_the_stock_edge_keeps_its_lift_and_its_reason`\n\nPositive pins:\n\n- `a_link_comes_in_from_the_air_to_a_piece_at_the_stock_edge`\n- `each_approach_of_the_bands_cuts_only_the_swath_of_its_piece`: each approach of the disc band and the dog-bone band is checked against the stock box of the case, not against the kernel's air.\n\nPins measured again, with no constant tuned:\n\n- `order_link::k4_link_rule_holds_and_each_lift_is_named`\n- `k4_order_link::kernel_order_and_link_round_the_disc_and_the_dog_bone` (it now also prints the places of the full-width feeds)\n- `k3_load::kernel_load_control_round_the_disc_and_the_dog_bone` (merged in PR #4265; it reads the same Outside plans)\n- `link_rule::a_link_leaves_a_cut_at_the_stock_edge_runs_in_the_air_and_comes_back_over_cleared_stock`: its first assertion pinned the old refusal. That link now stays as an approach.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Fixture (Auto / Inside / Outside) | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| disc pocket (law suite) | 0 / 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 / 0 |\n| disc band (law suite) | 13 / 0 / 13 | 0 / 0 / 0 |\n| dog-bone band (law suite) | 15 / 0 / 15 | 0 / 0 / 0 |\n| pocket with an island (law suite) | 7 / 7 / 5 | 7 / 7 / 5 |\n\n| Motion pin | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| disc, Inside | 0 lifts, 0 crossings | 0 lifts, 0 crossings |\n| disc, Outside | 13 lifts, 0 crossings; over 402, worst 145, full 0 | 0 lifts, 0 crossings; over 415, worst 145, full 0 |\n| dog bone, Inside | 0 lifts, 0 crossings | 0 lifts, 0 crossings |\n| dog bone, Outside | 15 lifts, 0 crossings; over 724, worst 167, full 0 | 0 lifts, 0 crossings; over 739, worst 180, full 1 |\n\nThe record's target of 0 lifts on the disc is met. No lift stays on the disc.\n\nOn the dog bone one approach arrives at full width, at (-2.40, 25.00) on the top stock edge. The material is in the swath of the next piece. Thus it is not a gouge and not stock off the curve. But no stage reads that load yet, because the load stage reads the cuts and not the links. Follow-up: #4272.\n\nThe K3 rows (moves above the limit, worst degrees, unnamed moves) change on Outside only. Disc: none 402/145/13 to 415/145/19; constant 334/118/74 to 344/122/81. Dog bone: none 724/167/3 to 739/180/13; constant 678/143/66 to 683/143/69. The decision record has the table.\n\n## Decision\n\n`docs/decisions/4254-kernel-air-approach.md`. Summary:\n\n- The approach is the last stretch of a proved stay link. It is not a lift-free re-entry step.\n- The proof uses the area of the swept disc.\n- The way to the air uses the three tries of K4.\n- The order stage needs no new rule, because the direction fixes the start of an open piece and the walk already asks the link stage for a proved path.\n\nDropped: a new plan step, a tangent approach, an arc lead.\n\n## Gate (final head)\n\n- `cargo check --tests -p camcraft-pathkernel`, then `-p camcraft-motion`: ok.\n- `camcraft-pathkernel` `laws`: 140 passed.\n- `camcraft-motion` `kernel_laws`: 30 passed.\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` on both crates: ok.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/side/path-kernel`: 4 steps ok (pathkernel build, lib, laws; motion kernel_laws).\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base origin/side/path-kernel`: 7 steps ok.\n- The branch merges `origin/side/path-kernel` at df9ec30b6 (PR #4265) without a conflict.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No planner calls the link stage yet. Thus the output of the old planners is identical. The example catalog suites were not run, because no post and no planner toolpath changes.\n- The engagement of the approach is not controlled (#4272).\n- Stock edges that are not straight were tested only with the tooth fixture. Inch units and work planes other than XY were not tested.\n- The test file `air_approach.rs` joins the `laws` directory suite. No new top-level test binary.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #4254\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
